  "evidence_classification": "inconclusive",
  "interpretation": "In the TB-A07 three-reference transfer context, explicit reference-role declarations did not improve the registered primary cross_reference_leakage_control dimension because both conditions scored 5.00, producing a variant-minus-control delta of 0.00. The explicit-role condition did improve semantic_compliance from 4.00 to 5.00 and reference_role_fidelity from 4.00 to 5.00, while aesthetic quality and technical cleanliness were unchanged. The overall mean increased from 4.60 to 5.00. EXP-014 is classified inconclusive because the leakage-control metric was already saturated at the maximum score in the control condition, leaving no discriminatory range with which to observe the hypothesized leakage reduction.",
